From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:21:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: a session has an id and a name

A Space's profile_id has been the storage-partition name of its own session.
It is now the id of a session, which several Spaces may hold. The id is the
jar's token, so a session needs no second key and nothing on disk moves.

The name lives in one new list, stedding.spaces.sessions, and only for a session
made with a name, joined by a second Space, or left by its last Space. A token
with no row is a session named after the Space that holds it, which is every
Independent session on disk today. Nothing is rewritten, so there is no
migration to fail, and an older build reads every Space as it was.

SpacePartitionNames reads the list as well as the Spaces, so the collection and
Delete browsing data reach a session no Space uses (sessions S37, S43, S44).

Why: Arc's users keep several Spaces on one sign-in, and two have asked for it
here (BACKLOG S-272, GitHub issue 8, ADR 0032).

Removable when: Chromium gives a profile more than one set of sign-ins of its
own, which it has no plan to.
